{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"I raised the `rate` service's throttle limit, restarted `search`, and submitted the mitigation. The submission was accepted. I can't yet say whether end-user requests are healthy, because validation runs after submit.\n\n- **Cause:** The `rate` deployment was throttled to `RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT=20` with a queue capacity of 256. `search` calls `rate`, and those calls were failing with `DeadlineExceeded` and `ResourceExhausted`. `search` also retries up to 3 times, which adds more load on `rate`.\n- **Fix:** I set `RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT=2000` and `RATE_QUEUE_CAPACITY=4096` on `deploy/rate`.\n- **Restart:** After the `rate` rollout, `search` briefly logged `Unavailable` errors from `rate`. I restarted `search` and it came up registered in consul.\n- **Check:** After the restart, `search` and `rate` showed no new errors in their logs. I did not run a load test."}}
